# Grocery List App - Project Overview

This project is an offline-first Android grocery/shopping list app focused on Sri Lankan users.

## Non-negotiable product goals
- All core list and shopping features must work without internet.
- No login, no backend, and no developer-owned analytics in MVP.
- Grocery data is stored locally using Room/SQLite.
- Provide useful default Sri Lankan grocery items on first launch.
- Support fast pre-shopping selection, then focused shopping checklist flow.
- Support category and store-type grouping for clarity in-store.
- Support favorites and frequently purchased items for faster repeat use.
- Support sharing via Android share sheet, including WhatsApp.
- Monetize only with small non-intrusive AdMob banner ads.
- Keep UI simple, fast, readable, and usable on older Android phones.

## Explicitly out of scope
- Cloud sync
- User accounts
- Firebase Analytics
- Location tracking
- Contacts access
- SMS reading
- Camera/barcode scanning
- Full-screen ads
- Interstitial ads
- Complex budgeting features

## Decision guardrails
- Choose the simplest implementation that preserves offline reliability.
- If a feature increases complexity but not everyday shopper speed, defer it.
- Prefer predictable local behavior over clever but fragile UX patterns.
- Avoid dependencies that require network for core usage.

